+## Channel design system (PROPOSED 2026-10-27; applies only after owner approval; full spec docs/design-system.md)
+Supersedes the DARK-stage identity and look rules 1 and 3 of the Reference doctrine below; the storytelling rules stay.
+- Stage: CELESTE studio seamless (#8FD6F2 top to #62B4DC bottom), gentle contact shadow, no vignette, no halo. Hero keeps REAL colours on a
+  navy plinth (#2B4C70). Constant for every drawn-style video.
+- Ink: navy #0B2540. Accent (active quantity): ember #E8590C. Error: #C92A2A. Subtitles: navy words, the spoken word reversed in a navy
+  box with white text (15.5:1), 4 px white outline on the others. Overlay text/graphics follow factory/overlays.THEMES["light"].
+- Safe zones (1080x1920): captions centred at y=0.24H (above the 288 px top reserve); hero and graphics inside y 0.15-0.75, x 0.10-0.90;
+  nothing needed to read below y=0.75 (platform UI) or right of x=0.82 below y=0.45 (button stack). Counters at y<=0.72.
+- Typography: Montserrat ExtraBold; scale in docs/design-system.md. Cost: celeste lighting renders ~1.4-1.75x the dark looks (tuned
+  96-128 spp, adaptive 0.03-0.05, 4 bounces); measured, never guessed.
+- Brand: name and handle per docs/design-system.md once chosen; mark and end card rendered in code (tools/brand_mark.py).
 
